Chapter One: The Ancestors of Jesus Christ
These are the names of the ancestors of Jesus Christ, son of David, son of Abraham:
Ibrahim son of Ishaq, and Ishaq son of Yaqub, and Yaqub son of Judah and his brothers,
And Judah begot Perez and Zerah by Tamar, and Perez begot Hezron, and Hezron begot Aram,
Aram was the son of Aminadab, Aminadab was the son of Nahshon, and Nahshon was the son of Salmon,
Salmon was born to Boaz from Rahab, and Boaz was born to Obed from Ruth, and Obed was born to Jesse.
And Jesse begot King David. And David begot Solomon by the woman who had been the wife of Uriah,
And Solomon was the son of Rehoboam, and Rehoboam was the son of Abijah, and Abijah was the son of Asa,
Asa begot Jehoshaphat, and Jehoshaphat begot Joram, and Joram begot Uzziah,
And Hezekiah begot Manasseh, Manasseh begot Amon, and Amon begot Josiah,
And Hezekiah begot Manasseh, and Manasseh begot Amos, and Amos begot Josiah,
And Josiah was born in Kenaniah and his brothers at the time when the Jews were exiled in the land of Babylon.
And after they returned to the Jews from Babylon, Jeconiah begot Shealtiel, and Shealtiel begot Zerubbabel,
And Zerubbabel begot Abiud, and Abiud begot Eliakim, and Eliakim begot Azor,
And Azor was the son of Zadok, and Zadok was the son of Achim, and Achim was the son of Eliud,
Eliud was the father of Eleazar, Eleazar was the father of Matthan, and Matthan was the father of Jacob,
And Jacob was the father of Joseph, the husband of Mary, who gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Messiah.
All the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations, and from David until the time they were exiled to Babylon are fourteen generations. And from the time they were exiled to Babylon until the birth of Christ are fourteen generations. The birth of Jesus Christ
This is how the birth of Jesus Christ came about: When Mary was betrothed to Joseph, before they came together, she was found to be with child through the Holy Spirit. Luke
