And Jesus answered them, saying: "God has sent me only to the lost sheep of the house of Israel."
But that woman came, prostrated to him, and said: "Help me, my master!"
He answered her and said: "It's not right to take the children's bread and throw it to the dogs."
And the woman said to him: "Yes, sir! But even the dogs eat from the scraps that fall from the tables of their owners."
And Jesus answered her, saying: "Your faith is great, oh woman! It will be done for you as you wish." And at that moment, her daughter was healed. Many people are healed.
And afterwards, Jesus went from there to the side of the Sea of Galilee, and went up the mountain and sat there.
Many groups of people came to him, including the lame, the blind, the crippled, the paralyzed, the lepers, and many others, and he placed them at his feet and healed them.
And the groups of people were amazed because they saw the lame walking, the crippled being healed, the lepers being cleansed, the blind seeing, and they gave glory to God of Israel. Jesus fed four thousand.
And Jesus called his disciples and said to them: "Stay with these people, because they have been with me for three days, and they have nothing to eat. I do not want to send them away hungry so that they do not faint on the way."
And they said to his students: "Where are we going to get bread in this wilderness to feed such a large group?"
And Jesus said to them, "How many loaves do you have?" They answered him, "Seven loaves and some small fish."
And Jesus commanded the crowd of people to sit on the ground,
And God took those seven loaves and fishes, gave thanks, broke them, and gave them to His disciples, and the disciples gave them to the crowds of people.
They all ate until they were full, and they carried seven sacks full of the pieces of bread they had torn.
And there were people who ate a quarter of a thousand each, excluding women and children.
And when Jesus sent the crowds away, he got into the boat and went to the region of Magadan.
Chapter: Signs of the Times
Some of the Pharisees and Sadducees came to Jesus to test him, and they asked him to show them a sign from heaven. Matthew
But he answered them and said: "When the sun sets, you say: the weather will be clear, because the sky is red.
And early in the morning they say: today it will rain, because the sky is red and cloudy. You can interpret the weather, but you cannot interpret the signs of the times!
"An evil and adulterous generation asks for a sign, but no sign will be given to it except the sign of Jonah." And after that, Jesus left them and went away. Matthew 12:39; Luke 11:29 The yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees
