Chapter Seventeen: Jesus Appears in His Glory
And after six days, Jesus took Peter and James and his brother John, and led them up alone to a high mountain.
And his appearance changed before them, and his face shone like the sun, and his clothes became dazzling, shining like light.
And it appears to them that Moses and Elijah are talking with Jesus.
Peter said to Jesus: "How good it is for us to stay here, Lord. If you want, I will make three tents here, one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah."
And when he was speaking, a bright cloud overshadowed them, and a voice came from the cloud, saying: "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear him!" 2 Peter 1:17,18
